# ── design-system-rails · Sprint 1 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The APPROVED prototype, byte-for-byte. `APPROVED.md` records the approval as this file's SHA-256,
# and states that a changed hash with no new approval line means the design is UNAPPROVED. Prettier
# reformatting it would silently do exactly that — the design would become unapproved because a
# formatter ran. `tokens.test.ts` asserts the hash, so this is belt and braces on purpose.
apps/web/design-system/console-prototype.html

# GENERATED from that prototype by `extract-css.mjs`, under a do-not-hand-edit header, and checked
# by `--check` in CI. Prettier and the generator disagree about CSS value spacing
# (`cubic-bezier(.2,0,.2,1)` vs `cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0.2, 1)`), so leaving these in prettier's
# scope means one of the two rewrites the file and the other fails the build — a deadlock where the
# only way out is to stop running one of them. The generator wins because its output is derived from
# an approved artefact; prettier's job is source a human types.
apps/web/design-system/tokens.css
apps/web/design-system/tokens.ts
apps/web/design-system/reference.css
apps/web/design-system/coverage.json

# ── mockups-as-built · Story 1.1 / 1.3 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The same deadlock as the four above, for the same reason. `STATE-CONTRACT.json` is generated from
# the approved prototype by `state-contract.mjs` and checked by `--check` in CI; `STATE-MATCH.json`
# is written by the visual gate itself and is the floor the ratchet reads. Both carry a
# do-not-hand-edit header. Prettier and `JSON.stringify(…, 2)` disagree about where short arrays
# wrap, so leaving them in prettier's scope means the formatter rewrites the file and the generator
# then fails the build — verified, not assumed: `format:changed --write` reflowed STATE-CONTRACT.json
# and `state-contract.mjs --check` went red on the next command.
apps/web/design-system/STATE-CONTRACT.json
apps/web/design-system/STATE-MATCH.json

